[Music]  Katherine McNamara opens up about the  emotional experience filming the  Shadowhunters series finale I think the  biggest gift that we had was being able  to shoot a series finale you know we got  a - I think maybe two and a half hour  now that it's edited together movie  basically that's going to air at the end  of the season and it's it was so  gratifying and and I will be eternally  grateful for having that chance to  really say goodbye and them in the right  way and in a way that does justice to  this world into these characters that  we've all worked so hard to build it was  I guess my favorite part of it was  probably seeing not only the cast and  the writers and everything but our crew  as well who's been with us most of them  since day one really get to have a  little bit of artistry with it and let  loose because we're making it not only  for the fans but also for us to sort of  complete that journey and express for  one last time what we loved so much this  is who I am  join me I didn't steal anything I can  honestly say I didn't steal one thing  but I did I was able to take home a few  things I have a set of Clarice swords  and a stelae and a few pieces of  wardrobe but also our you know like I  said we're very much a family there our  camera crew has been with us our camera  operators and they're there folks have  been with us since day one and right  after we shot the last scene in Clara's  bedroom they took one of the you know  the wooden artists dummy molds that you  can kind of move about there was one on  Clara's bookshelf always and they all  signed it and gave it to me after we had  wrapped that set as they were tearing it  down and it's I have it on my dresser at  home now and it's just something that  allow me to keep with me always a  fashionista Katherine looks stunning  when she spoke with et at the daily  front Rose fashion la Awards daily front  row it's just it's a great outlet that  always sums up fashion both in their  ready-to-wear and the high-fashion side  it kind of combines everything and it's  one of those outlets that's always been  very kind to me so I'm happy to come out  and support I've always loved fashion in  the sense that it's a way to express  your inner self on the outside without  having to say a word and it's a way to  kind of express your whether it's your  mood or who you are as a human being to  the world in a way that's very artistic  and and you know since I was a little  girl I've loved playing dress-up but  I've always loved putting together my  own outfit and it's sometimes more it's  been more successful than others over  the years but it's it's always a lot of  fun and something I very much  appreciated  [Music]

